This product includes software and data from the following sources:

DATA SOURCES
  - US Census Bureau, American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates
    (county population, MSA labels). https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs
  - Move United, public Adaptive Sports Chapter directory (display-only,
    never load-bearing in similarity matching).
    https://moveunitedsport.org
  - Public Team USA roster data, 2016-2024, Olympic + Paralympic
    combined (athlete names dropped at the aggregation step per the
    project's NIL hard rule).
  - NFHS Athletics Participation Survey (high school participation
    context). https://www.nfhs.org
  - HUD USPS ZIP-to-County crosswalk (ZIP input → county FIPS
    resolution). https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/usps_crosswalk.html
  - NOAA nClimGrid 5km gridded climate (county-level temperature +
    precipitation aggregates). https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/land-based-station/nclimgrid

INFRASTRUCTURE + KEY DEPENDENCIES
  - Google Cloud Run (frontend + backend hosting)
  - Vertex AI Gemini 2.5 Flash (narrative + Q&A generation)
  - FastAPI (Sebastián Ramírez, MIT) — backend HTTP framework
  - React + Vite + TypeScript — frontend stack (multiple authors, MIT)
  - react-simple-maps + us-atlas — geographic visualization (MIT)
  - react-scrollama — scrollytelling orchestrator (MIT)
  - Tailwind CSS — design system primitives (MIT)
  - Pydantic — schema validation (MIT)
  - pandas, pyarrow, numpy — data pipeline (BSD-3-Clause)

Full dependency licenses are available via:
  - frontend: `npm ls --all` after `npm ci` in `frontend/`
  - backend: `pip-licenses` after `pip install -r requirements.txt`
